anges\n\n### **`/app/analyze_climate_modern.py`** - Modernized Analysis Script\nKey improvements over the legacy code:\n\n**Python 3 Syntax & APIs:**\n- ✅ `configparser` (Python 3) instead of deprecated `ConfigParser`\n- ✅ `plt.subplots()` instead of deprecated `plt.figure()` + `add_subplot()`\n- ✅ `.groupby()` with modern iteration (no `iteritems()`)\n- ✅ F-strings instead of `%` formatting\n- ✅ `Exception as e` syntax instead of Python 2's `except Exception, e:`\n\n**Modern Libraries:**\n- ✅ `pathlib.Path` for cross-platform file handling\n- ✅ Pandas with UTF-8 encoding support\n- ✅ Proper datetime parsing without deprecated `date_parser` parameter\n- ✅ NumPy modern array operations\n\n**Features:**\n- Reads CSV with proper UTF-8 encoding\n- Processes both stations (101, 102) from the data\n- Calculates mean temperature per station\n- Output format: `\"Station {id} mean temperature: {value:.1f}°C\"`\n- Generates visualizations for temperature anomalies\n\n### **`/app/requirements.txt`** - Dependency Specification\n```\nnumpy>=1.20.0\npandas>=1.3.0\nmatplotlib>=3.5.0\nscipy>=1.7.0\n```\n\n**Test Results:**\n```\nStarting climate analysis...\nStation 101 mean temperature: -15.5°C\nStation 102 mean temperature: 30.3°C\nAnalysis completed successfully!\n```\n\nThe modernized code is production-ready and works with Python 3.8+.","ttft_ms":3246,"type":"result","duration_ms":30298,"uuid":"39df8568-031e-4190-ac64-c332cb1c99d0","ttft_stream_ms":1014,"time_to_request_ms":81,"queued_turn_count":0}
